      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another issue with this code (unrelated to this change) is that the `glob` doesn\u0027t guarantee traversal order. What we need is a guaranteed depth-first traversal, which ensures that a parent directory is visited after all of its child directories are visited. This ensures removal of the parent dir if all child directories were empty. With a random traversal order this is not guaranteed.\nFor example, if we have the following all empty directories:\n```\nrefs/changes/45/12345/meta\nrefs/changes/45/12345/1\nrefs/changes/45/12345/2\n```\n\nthen `refs/changes/45/12345/` will only be detected as empty if all of its childred are processed first.\n\nTo achieve that we shall use `os.walk(root_path, topdown\u003dFalse)`. The `topdown\u003dFalse` guarantees depth-first traversal.",
      "revId": "0e877e79d9b73535722cc265f21b1f89c3e0da45",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
